      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 34. बृहस्पति—from बृहत् speech + पति the lord of; here the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "planet Jupiter, तद्बृहतोः करपत्योश्चोरदेवतयोः सुट् तलोपश्च’ Vàrt. on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Pán. VI. I. 157. स् is substituted for the final of बृहत् and तत्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "when followed by पति and कर when the sense is a particular",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "deity and a thief respectively; so तत् + कर=तस्कर. संभाविताः—well",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "respected or esteemed i. e. of middle size.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "विशेष०—see com; or विशेष्यत इति विशेषः unusual, uncommon; or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "शिष्यते इति शेषः । विगतः शेषः यस्य complete, hence uncommon; विशेष-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "विक्रमः विशेष० तत्र रुचिः यस्य bent on performing deeds of unusual",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "valour. वैरायते A denom. from वैर meaning वैरं करोति; derived",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with the aff. क्यङ्; see com. भास्वरौ brilliant. भ्रान्तः—v. l. revol-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ving; कर्तरि क्तः by गत्यर्थाकर्मक &c. Pan. III. 4, 72. पर्वन्—The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "time of new or full moon (opposition or conjunction). शीर्षाव०-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "The allusion here is to the severance of the demon’s head at the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "time when the nectar that was churned out of the ocean was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "served to the gods, and Ráhu attempted to drink it by joining",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "their line. The sun and the moon informed Vishnu of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "fraud, whereupon he severed the demon’s head with his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "discus. But as the demon had tasted a little quantity of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "amrita the head lived and is supposed to wreak its vengeance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "on the two luminaries. See Mat. Pu. Adh. II. 5. 13. 16. Bhág.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "P. VIII. 9. 23–26, The fig is अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा as the action of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "Ráhu which is not the matter in hand (अप्रस्तुत) implies the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "action of an inveterate wicked man which is the matter intended",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "to be described.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl, 35. फणाफलक The flat surface of (extensive board for-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "med by ) his hoods. Comp. Mat. Pu. CCLIX. 7. मध्येपृष्ठम्—on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the back. Avy. Comp. This is less common though by no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "means very rare: comp. Bv. I. 60; Nai. III. 40; Sis III, 70",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "VI. 22 and 70 Bhatti V. 4. पारे मध्ये षष्ठ्या वा । Pân. II.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "1. 18. The words पार and मध्य are optionally compounded",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "with a noun in the gen. case forming an Avy., the final अ of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "these being irregularly (निपातनात् एदन्तत्वं चानयोर्निपात्यते । Sid.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "Kau.) changed to ए; optionally there may be Gen. Tat. e. g.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Line 1 '35.' has faded '5'; Line 5 'VI. 22' is badly broken; Line 10 'Kau.)' has faded '. )'"
    },
